// Hitsplat types (cache config group 32).
//
// Hand-authored, because OpenRune's gameval table has no hitsplat namespace —
// but not guessed. Each id was resolved to its sprite through the config
// record's opcode 5 and the sprite's dominant colour measured:
//
//   0  sprite 2270  rgb  61, 31,126  blue   the zero/block splat
//   1  sprite 3521  rgb 142, 21, 26  red    ordinary damage
//   3  sprite 1361  rgb 153,109,  4  yellow
//   4  sprite 1633  rgb 151,108,  3  yellow
//   5  sprite 1632  rgb  26, 78, 73  teal
//   6  sprite 1629  rgb 104, 21,140  purple
//   7  sprite 3405  rgb  61, 99, 19  green  poison
//
// The mock had 0 and 1 the other way round, so every hit drew the blue block
// splat and every miss drew the red one. Nothing failed — it just looked wrong,
// which is why it needed measuring rather than reasoning about.
//
// The unnamed ids (2, 8-77) are real records; most carry no sprite at all. They
// get symbols when something needs them.
0=hitsplat_block
1=hitsplat_damage
3=hitsplat_yellow
4=hitsplat_yellow_alt
5=hitsplat_teal
6=hitsplat_purple
7=hitsplat_poison
